Chapter: ReturnNarrowProven

 Checker-prover reach, post-campaign (BoundedSignatures.md): two new
 proof doors. A call to a function with a DECLARED bounded return
 proves that range inside arithmetic - sound because the stage-B
 postcondition guard enforces the declared return at runtime - so
 10 + clamp100 raw lands in 10..110, inside 0..255 (CDX2053). A
 let-local whose value's resolved type is a bounded IntegerTy
 carries the type's range, so 255 - v proves when v carries a
 field's 0..255. text-length joins the structural builtin facts.
 The sidecars pin the proofs and the runtime values.

Section: Definitions

  Meter = record {
   level : Integer between 0 and 255
  }

  Tally = record {
   chars : Integer between 0 and 4294967295
  }

  clamp100 : Integer -> Integer between 0 and 100
  clamp100 (v) = __narrow (if v < 0 then 0 else if v > 100 then 100 else v)

  fill : Integer -> Meter
  fill (raw) = Meter { level = 10 + clamp100 raw }

  invert-level : Meter -> Meter
  invert-level (m) =
   let v = m.level
   in Meter { level = 255 - v }

  count-chars : Text -> Tally
  count-chars (s) = Tally { chars = text-length s }

Section: Main

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
   print-line-uni (integer-to-text ((fill 50).level))
   print-line-uni (integer-to-text ((invert-level (fill 50)).level))
   print-line-uni (integer-to-text ((count-chars "codex").chars))
  end
